= [$] Evolving the LAVD scheduler from gaming to servers
[Kernel] Posted Oct 7, 2026 13:33 UTC (Wed) by corbet
The [43]extensible scheduler class, which enables the
creation of custom CPU schedulers with BPF, has led to a
burst of innovation in this area; [44]the LAVD scheduler
has, perhaps, been one of the most noteworthy schedulers
to emerge. Though it was originally [45]designed for
gaming applications, the LAVD scheduler has since grown to
serve other types of workloads as well. At the 2026
edition of [46]Kernel Recipes, Changwoo Min and Gavin Guo
presented an overview of this scheduler and how it has
evolved over time. 
